course: dictionary
lesson: 15914
title: Un- words and what they mean
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word unpainted is made of three parts: un- means not, paint is the colour you put on things, and -ed shows that something has been done to it. Put them together and unpainted means not covered with paint.
explain: «The wooden birdhouse was unpainted, so we could see the plain grain of the wood.» The clue is that the wood has no paint on it. It looks plain and natural, not bright or shiny.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The wooden birdhouse had no paint on it, so we could see the plain grain of the wood.» It still makes sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: Un- at the start of a word often means not, as in unhappy, undone and unpainted.
fact: «Unpainted» means not covered with paint.
fact: In design and technology lessons you may work with «unpainted wood» or an «unpainted model» before you add colour.
fact: In everyday life, an unpainted fence or wall is bare, with no colour on it.
fact: In maths, a cube may be painted on some faces and unpainted on others, so you have to count the faces carefully.
exercise: «The unpainted fence was grey and bare.» What does unpainted mean? | Freshly washed | Covered in lots of bright colours | Very old and broken | *Not covered with paint
exercise: A wooden cube is painted red on four faces and unpainted on the rest. How many faces are unpainted? | 0 | 4 | *2 | 6
exercise: Which word in «The unpainted model sat on the shelf» means not covered with paint? | the | shelf | sat | *unpainted
test: «The art teacher gave us unpainted pots to decorate.» What does unpainted mean here? | Broken into pieces | *Not covered with paint yet | Covered in glitter | Painted twice
test: Un- often means not. What does unfair mean? | Fairly | *Not fair | Fair again | Very fair
exam: Ella says the shed is unpainted. What does she mean? | It is being painted right now | Covered in bright paint | It is very old and dusty | *It has no paint on it
